# Inequalities solution path

Final wording for «אין» and «כל x» is the shared wording in tutoring-behavior.

## Linear

Same moves as a linear equation.

The inequality sign flips only when both sides are multiplied or divided by a negative number. Moving a term does not flip the sign. Multiplying or dividing by a positive number does not flip the sign.

Strict and weak inequalities stay strict or weak.

## AND and OR

Solve each condition if it is not already a domain.

Drawing on the number line is optional. A correct final domain is accepted without a drawing. If a drawing was started, Hint and Next Step continue that drawing. They do not require it when the student goes straight to the domain.

AND is the intersection. OR is the union.

## Quadratic

Arrange so one side is 0. Find the zeros with the quadratic path.

Two student-valid ways to read the sign:

- Parabola: mark the zeros and sketch the parabola, then read where it is above or below the x-axis.
- Sign check: mark the zeros, pick a test number in each interval, substitute, and keep the intervals with the right sign.

If the student has started one of these, Hint and Next Step stay on it.

If neither has started, Full Solution uses the parabola.

Special cases stay: two zeros, a double zero, no zeros, every x, no solution, and a single point when the inequality includes equality.

A zero is inside the solution only for ≤ or ≥. It is outside the solution for < or >.

No zeros does not by itself mean no solution. The sign still has to be checked.
